<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The brand mark at splash size. It holds no geometry: it is drawable/ic_launcher_foreground
  drawn larger, so the mark can never drift between the launcher and the splash the way it
  did when the two pointed at different files.

  The scale is here rather than in the mark itself because the two surfaces want different
  sizes. The launcher foreground is sized against the 72dp window a launcher shows, which
  deliberately leaves room inside the 66dp safe circle; the splash has no such neighbours,
  and at that size the mark read small and soft in the middle of a full-screen indigo field.
  Android's splash guidance is an icon of 288dp whose content sits inside a 192dp circle —
  two thirds of the canvas — and the mark's own extent is 48.9 of 108, so it was filling
  about two thirds of the room it had.

  The inset is negative, which expands rather than pads: -15% a side scales by 1.30, landing
  the mark at 63.6 of 108 (88% of that circle) with the stroke thickening in proportion.
  Fractions are resolved against the bounds the platform hands this drawable, so it follows
  whatever icon size the device uses instead of assuming 288dp.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"
    android:inset="-15%" />
